+kind: persistence-change
+---
+
+# 2026-11-09-external-turn-ownership
+
+English | [中文](2026-11-09-external-turn-ownership.zh.md)
+
+## Summary
+
+Records the engine and serialized admission for an externally owned turn.
+
+## Table of Contents
+
+- [Declaration](#declaration)
+- [Compatibility](#compatibility)
+- [Verification](#verification)
+- [Dev Note](#dev-note)
+
+<a id="declaration"></a>
+## Declaration
+
+```yaml persistence-change
+schemaVersion: 1
+id: 2026-11-09-external-turn-ownership
+baseline: false
+changes:
+  - root: "event:turn/owner"
+    previous: null
+    after: "6c18d530ae7cba12956444baaa0ba50a2ab08d9d69dd38725415eeee7bb19472"
+    decision: same-version
+```
+
+<a id="compatibility"></a>
+## Compatibility
+
+The V4 header and existing event schemas are unchanged. An older reader refuses the required turn/owner event before interpretation or repair, preserving the original bytes. A reader supporting ownership preserves an unclosed owned turn for its engine. Ordinary turns retain their existing recovery rules.
+
+<a id="verification"></a>
+## Verification
+
+Read and write opens using the unchanged V4 reader with the baseline event catalogue refused an actual owned log with both complete and torn tails, preserving bytes and inodes in all four cases. The current reader passed five Node process-exit recovery cases using JSONL and SQLite, including cancellation without model calls and an uncertain write that was never replayed.
+
+<a id="dev-note"></a>
+## Dev Note
+
+None.
