+## External turn execution
+
+The initial accepted input includes its bound prompt assembly and model selection. An engine handling the turn returns its ending. A listener that delegates through the waterfall keeps the standard loop. The [Agent API](../../packages/core/agent/README.md#intercept-or-observe-work-in-flight) describes ownership and recovery.
+
+```ts type-equiv
+/** Input admitted through the host's inbox, prompt assembly and pre-step policy. */
+type TurnInput =
+  | { kind: 'reject' }
+  | {
+    kind: 'enter'
+    messages: UserMessage[]
+    assembly: PromptAssembly
+    /** Captured route selection; no implicit re-selection during external execution. */
+    selection: Readonly<ModelSelection>
+    startsRequestSeries?: true
+  }
+```
+
+```ts type-equiv
+/** A delegated engine's completed turn; undefined delegates to the standard loop. */
+type TurnExecutionResult = { reason: TurnEndReason } | undefined
+```
+
 ## Sessions
 
 A `Session` is an **append-only log** of typed `SessionEvent`s — the single source of truth. The LLM message history is *derived* from the log (`deriveMessages()`), not stored separately. Every entry carries a monotonic `seq`, a `time`, and a `type`-discriminated `data` payload; surface variants may also list cited earlier events in `sourceEventSeqs` and carry a `surfaceOp`.
