+
+# External-turn ownership
+
+English | [中文](guide.zh.md)
+
+## Change
+
+External engines can persist a required `turn/owner` event before executing a turn. Builds that do not recognize it refuse the Session log. The format header is unchanged because the required-event discriminator prevents unsafe interpretation. Existing logs without ownership records remain readable; this does not grant older builds permission to resume owned turns.
+
+## Migration
+
+1. Upgrade every reader and writer that accesses owned sessions to a build supporting `turn/owner` and `agent.externalTurns`.
+2. Keep the engine that claimed each admission available. Its recovery handler must validate and resume the original admission; it must not start another turn or replay an uncertain write.
+3. Before rollback, stop external execution and retain the original Session and engine ledger. Do not delete or mark ownership records ignorable to make an older reader accept them.
+4. Confirm an interrupted owned turn resumes with its original identity and that a missing engine leaves it recoverable without calling the default model loop.
