 ### Turn and step flow
 
+Before the first standard step, `agent/execute-turn` lets an external engine own all model and tool steps while this driver retains turn boundaries, cancellation, and status. `externalTurns.claim()` appends a required `turn/owner` admission; the engine must flush it before effects. Cold resume preserves that owned open tail instead of appending an interrupted closer. `externalTurns.resume()` admits only the recorded owner and settles the original turn once; an execution failure retains ownership and does not drain queued prompts through the standard loop. See the [Session compatibility migration](../../../docs/upgrade-guide/v0.2.2-rc.1/external-turn-ownership/guide.md) before opening these logs with an older build.
